    ``Wb == 0`` are omitted; for each retained bin ``ob = Tb / Wb`` and
    ``pb = Pb / Wb``. In ascending bin index order the components are

    ``reliability = fsum(Wb * (pb - ob) ** 2) / W``,
    ``resolution = fsum(Wb * (ob - o) ** 2) / W``, and
    ``uncertainty = o * (1 - o)``,

    each an exact zero normalized to ``0.0``. Overflow, invalid
    operations during the post-validation conversion or arithmetic,
    division by zero, and non-finite intermediate values or results
    raise FloatingPointError.

